# Shared server-side configuration for session chat, ghost text, and Azure voice.
# Copy to .env in the repository root and replace these placeholders.
AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT=https://YOUR-RESOURCE.openai.azure.com/openai/v1
AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY=YOUR-KEY
DEPLOYMENT_NAME=YOUR-DEPLOYMENT

# Only needed when the endpoint is a legacy resource root (without /openai/v1):
# AZURE_OPENAI_API_VERSION=2025-04-01-preview

# Optional Azure voice: uncomment and configure all four independently of text.
# Whisper is STT only; gpt-audio-mini generates spoken answers via Chat Completions,
# not /audio/speech TTS. The endpoint is a resource origin, with no /openai/v1 path.
# Or export SPEC_AZURE_VOICE_ENV_FILE=/absolute/path/to/private-voice.env
# in the local Rust server's launch environment, not in this dotenv file.
# That file replaces this shared file for Azure voice only; text settings stay unchanged.
# If unset, voice uses SPEC_AI_ENV_FILE or the nearest .env. Process voice exports
# override file values, even when empty. Restart the server and reload the browser.
# Invalid Azure voice config disables only Azure voice with a sanitized warning;
# shared text config errors still fail startup. Never put secrets in the browser.
# AZURE_OPENAI_VOICE_ENDPOINT=https://YOUR-RESOURCE.openai.azure.com
# AZURE_OPENAI_VOICE_API_KEY=YOUR-VOICE-KEY
# AZURE_OPENAI_WHISPER_DEPLOYMENT=spec-whisper
# AZURE_OPENAI_AUDIO_DEPLOYMENT=spec-audio-mini
# These example deployment names must exist on YOUR-RESOURCE; see docs/realtime.md.
# Old AZURE_OPENAI_REALTIME_* / SPEC_AZURE_REALTIME_ENV_FILE settings are no longer used.
